   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **One Big Holiday** (1 review): Third song in set, prompting desire for older tunes [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Wordless**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [10]\n- **It Beats**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [10]\n- **One Big**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [10]\n- **I Will Sing**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [10]\n- **Hell**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [10]\n- **I Wil Be There (Jim)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [10]\n- **Bermuda (Jim)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [10]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MMJ2005-11-23FMSBD.flacf** (recommended): FM broadcast; 20 songs; 111 min; rated 4.83/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Audio quality is superior to other available MMJ downloads; Radio broadcast origin results in fantastic sound quality; Band sounds pretty darn good in this recording [4][6][9]\n- **mmj2005-11-23.flac16**: source not stated; 20 songs; 114 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Band performed in Louisville on the day before Thanksgiving [3]\n- Audience members clapped rhythmically during the song Dondante [7]\n- Reviewers consider this the best MMJ recording currently available [5]\n- Listener prefers this show over the album Z [8]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MMJ2005-11-23FMSBD.flacf**: taped by Kory Johnson; transferred by Kory Johnson; source: FM Broadcast [1]. Also: Recorded from radio, with host banter removed between tracks; Guitar strum at start of Run Thru was edited [1]\n- **mmj2005-11-23.flac16**: source: Schoeps mk41 (DIN)> kc5> cmc6xt> Sonosax SX-M2> Apogee AD-1000> D8 @ 44.1k, ROW Q, 7 seats right of center [2]",
